        "captions": {
            "linkedin": "Poll: Which Screen-Time Rule Actually Works In Your House?\n\nI'm asking because I need help. \ud83d\ude4f\n\nMy daughter is two years old, and she can already tap through Netflix faster than I can unlock my phone. We've tried strict caps and flexible windows \u2014 both usually lasted about three days before she found the loopholes.\n\nSo let me ask you: What's one screen-time rule that actually sticks in your household? And more importantly, what makes it stick?\n\n- \ud83d\udcf1 X minutes per day \u2014 Hard cap on usage\n- \ud83d\udeab Screen-free during meals \u2014 Boundaries tied to routines\n- \ud83c\udfae Only together \u2014 Co-viewing everything\n- \ud83d\udca1 Earn screens with chores/activities \u2014 Tie usage to positive behavior\n- \u2728 Something else entirely\n\nNo judgment here. I'm genuinely curious what families have found that works \u2014 especially for younger kids where the stakes are less about addiction and more about development.\n\nDrop your answer AND any tips in the comments. \ud83d\ude0a\n\n#DigitalGuardian #DigitalParenting #DigitalSafety #ParentingTips",
